  "full_text": "I look fabulous with my new haircut, huh? Mr. God looks... What do you think, Mr. God? Mr. God says, fabulous. We didn't even need a hat because we got hairs. Mr. God says, hearts to trust, minds to rest. Cast your burden upon the Lord. He will sustain you. He will never allow the righteous to be shaken. God has entrusted us a great deal. He knows that we can do all things by His grace, so He's entrusting us to trust Him. Yet He knows our fears as well, otherwise He wouldn't reassure us so often of His presence. We feel hurt and alone, God assures us He cares. We feel anger is unfulfilled, God provides wisdom and strength. We feel ashamed, God grants forgiveness and comfort. We feel anxious, God promises to supply us with all our needs. May He give us ears to hear, hearts to trust, minds to rest in Him. Our God is uniquely and ultimately trustworthy.",
